<id/01/0168/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Starch"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300012959>, <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41534> ;
    skos:broader <id/sub/sub_cereals_gr_wd_q41534/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "(_Amidon_, _Fecule_, Fr.; _Stärke_, Germ.); is a white pulverulent substance, composed of microscopic spheroids, which are bags containing the amylaceous matter. It exists in a great many different plants, and varies merely in the form and size of its microscopic particles; as found in some plants, it consists of spherical particles 1/1000 of an inch in diameter; and in others, of ovoid particles, of 1/300 or 1/400 of an inch. It occurs, 1. in the seeds of all the acotyledinous plants, among which are the several species of corns, and those of other _gramineæ_; 2. in the round perennial tap roots, which shoot up an annual stem; [Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (Project Gutenberg #44562)]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_cereals_grains; processing_state=manufactured): Farinaceous preparations (macaroni, vermicelli, crackers/biscuit, starch, dextrine) belong with Cereals; other starch headings (htc:1561, htc:1572) are already here. Layer-1 observations: 202 rows, 1800–1897. Series: CSP_Canadian Trade and Navigation ×19; KEW_CUST 5 ×12; KEW_CUST 4 ×9; CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×162. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×165; CWTS (Hundredweights) ×12; (no unit) ×12; Hundredweights.Quarters.Pounds ×9. Top routes: Quebec → All Countries ×25; Quebec → Great Britain ×15; Quebec → Newfoundland ×13; Quebec QC → All Countries ×11."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0168" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Starch"@en ;
